## What
`dispatch.sh --role cross-lab-review` can now write a machine-readable review receipt for Undersketch's Tier 2 deploy verifier (bead mk-zek32, requested via mk-63ei2).

New flags (all five or none): `--repo OWNER/NAME --repo-id ID --pr N --head SHA --base SHA`. Dispatch computes head tree, expected merge tree (`git merge-tree --write-tree base head`) and `diff_sha256` (sha256 of raw `git diff --no-ext-diff --no-renames --binary base head` in the -C checkout) before any model runs, so a bad flag fails fast.

Receipt: `${CLAVAIN_REVIEW_RECEIPT_DIR:-~/.local/state/clavain/reviews}/<owner>__<repo>/<pr>-<head>.json`, mode 0600, exclusive create, never overwritten. Fields: role, repo, repo_id, pr, head_sha, head_tree, base_sha, expected_merge_tree, diff_stat, diff_sha256, producer_identity, reviewer_identity, validator_relationship, verdict (PASS | PASS WITH NOTES | BLOCK), policy_hash, dispatch_id, attempt_id, created_at. Self-contained: the #63 per-run JSONL is cross-reference only.

## Fail-safe
No receipt (and the run exits 1) for a same-lab or unknown-lab reviewer, a capacity-substitute review, a failed run, a missing policy hash, or no strict final `VERDICT:` line. Any non-pass verdict maps to BLOCK. Identities come from the run, not flags.

## Trust limit
Catches mistakes only: writer and verifier run as the same account. Dispositions and the post-merge addendum are separate files owned by other writers.

## Tests
`tests/shell/dispatch_review_receipt.bats` (7) plus all 220 `dispatch_*.bats` pass.

